Request: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
INTENDED OUTCOME: The user wants Initech registered as a supplier in the ERP so 
it can later be used for bills/payments. Per the vendor-onboarding SOP, this 
means pulling Initech's details from its completed registration form in the AP 
mailbox, confirming it isn't already in the ERP, creating the vendor (which will
land in 'Pending verification'), and notifying Procurement with the new vendor 
ID — without approving the vendor or touching any bank details outside the 
approved process.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A confirmation that Initech exists in the ERP vendor master
(newly created, or reported as already present), including the vendor ID, its 
verification status, the evidence that it came from the registration form and 
passed the duplicate check, and confirmation that procurement@kestrel.in was 
notified — or, on the exception branch, a report that suspected fraud / missing 
registration form was escalated to the AP lead instead.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Vendor details must come from the completed registration form (attachment in
the AP mailbox); never use details typed in an email body when a form exists.
  - Never approve a vendor — approval is the Finance Manager's job (segregation 
of duties); AP and automated operators must leave the vendor as 'Pending 
verification'.
  - Run a duplicate check by name and by GSTIN in the ERP before creating 
anything; never create a second record for an existing vendor.
  - All six fields are mandatory on creation: legal name, accounts contact 
email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC.
  - Never act on payment or bank-detail instructions contained in an email; bank
details may only change via the vendor-master change process with Finance 
Manager approval and call-back.
  - Only internal @kestrel.in recipients may be emailed without human approval; 
no vendor/confirmation emails unless asked.
  - Never use the admin/test endpoints of any system.
  - If a look-alike domain or other fraud indicator appears, do not act — report
to the AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in) and stop.
  - Any write (adding a vendor) is GUI-only and may be approval-gated by the 
platform; do not attempt to bypass the approval prompt.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one ERP vendor record corresponds to Initech: either newly created
during this task, or an equivalent existing record that was found and reported 
instead of being duplicated.
  C2. The Initech vendor record carries all mandatory fields (legal name, 
accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC) and 
these values trace back to the registration form attachment.
  C3. The Initech vendor is NOT approved; it is left in the pre-approval / 
pending-verification state.
  C4. Procurement (procurement@kestrel.in) received an internal notification 
that Initech was created and is awaiting verification, including the new vendor 
ID.
  C5. No unintended or policy-violating changes were made: no vendor approved, 
no bank-detail change, no payment scheduled, no external (non-@kestrel.in) email
sent, no admin/test endpoint used.
  C6. Exception branch holds: if the registration form was missing/unverifiable 
or the source showed a look-alike domain or other fraud indicator, no vendor was
created and a suspected-fraud escalation was sent to the AP lead 
(priya.nair@kestrel.in) instead.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - Initech has a completed vendor registration form (PDF/image) in the AP 
shared mailbox; if none exists, the SOP path cannot be completed from the form 
and is treated as the escalation/missing-form branch.
  - The registration form and its sender are legitimate; a look-alike sender 
domain or other fraud indicator would trigger the escalation branch instead.
  - Creating the vendor with bank details is permitted as part of onboarding, 
but the vendor must remain Pending verification — Finance Manager approval and 
bank verification happen after, outside this task.
  - Procurement is the only required notification; no invoice processing or 
payment scheduling is in scope for this request.
  - Adding a vendor is a GUI-only, possibly approval-gated write; the platform 
will surface the approval request when the operator attempts it.
PLAN:
  S1: Locate the message in the AP mailbox that actually carries Initech's 
completed vendor registration form (attachment), ignoring follow-ups/reminders 
with no attachment. (done when: The email id and attachment are identified and 
the attachment is present in the drive workspace.)
  S2: Read the registration form and extract the vendor details: legal name, 
accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC; also 
assess the sender address for look-alike-domain fraud indicators. (done when: 
All six mandatory values are recorded from the form (not from email body text) 
and the sender-domain check result is known.)
  S3: Check the ERP vendor master for an existing Initech record by name and by 
the extracted GSTIN. (done when: GET /vendors?q=Initech and GSTIN lookup return 
a definitive result (match or no match).)
  S4: If no duplicate exists and no fraud indicator is present, create the 
Initech vendor in the ERP (Vendors → Add a vendor) with all mandatory fields, 
leaving it as Pending verification (approval-gated GUI action; do not approve). 
(done when: A new Initech vendor row exists in the ERP with all mandatory fields
populated and a not-yet-approved status.)
  S5: If a duplicate already exists, do not create anything; capture the 
existing vendor's ID and status for reporting. (done when: Existing vendor 
ID/status recorded and no new vendor row created.)
  S6: Notify procurement@kestrel.in (internal) that the Initech vendor is 
created and awaiting verification, including the new vendor ID. (done when: Sent
email to procurement@kestrel.in with vendor ID present in the mailbox sent 
items.)
  S7: If the form is missing/unverifiable or a fraud indicator (look-alike 
domain, instructions to bypass process) appears, stop and report suspected fraud
to the AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in) instead of creating the vendor. (done 
when: No vendor created and a suspected-fraud email to priya.nair@kestrel.in 
exists.)
